$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
$h = "D:\GITHUB  Project\sangam-handoff"
$root = "D:\GITHUB  Project\Custom WorkFlow\.claude\worktrees\workspace-scan-resume-06b524\sangam"
$files = @(
  "sangam-compliance/src/main/java/org/sangam/compliance/ComplianceAudit.java",
  "sangam-compliance/src/main/java/org/sangam/compliance/breach/IncidentReportingService.java",
  "sangam-compliance/src/main/java/org/sangam/compliance/breach/BreachIncidentService.java"
)
$parts = @()
foreach ($f in $files) {
  $hash = (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 (Join-Path $root $f)).Hash.Substring(0,16)
  $parts += "sangam/$f (before $hash)"
}
$parts += "NEW sangam/sangam-compliance/src/test/java/org/sangam/compliance/breach/SecurityIncidentCatalogueEventsH2Test.java"
$ts = [DateTime]::UtcNow.ToString("yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssZ")
$claim = "$ts B61 CLAIM W4-A decision 299 (security catalogue events, sangam-compliance; no live claim on these files, last B46 W3-E released 2026-11-12T12:07:26Z): " + ($parts -join " ; ")
Add-Content -Encoding UTF8 -Path "$h\FILE-CLAIMS.md" -Value $claim
$change = "$ts | W4-A/B61 | CHANGE | Decision 299 under claim $ts in sangam-compliance. ComplianceAudit gains the catalogue names SEC_INCIDENT_OPENED, SEC_INCIDENT_CLASSIFIED, SEC_REPORT_SUBMITTED, SEC_INCIDENT_CLOSED (and DPDP_BREACH_REPORTED once the INFO below is answered), each appended on the organisation chain cmp:<tenant> through AuditChain in the caller's transaction, next to the existing CMP_INCIDENT_* event (same pattern as decision 301: the catalogue event and the specific one). IncidentReportingService.register writes SEC_INCIDENT_OPENED (incident, authority, noticedAt, dueAt, breach, actor) and SEC_INCIDENT_CLASSIFIED (incident, authority, type code and label from the authority catalogue, personalDataLikely, personalData = linked to a breach, actor); the type is classified and checked at registration, there is no separate classify step today. submit writes SEC_REPORT_SUBMITTED (incident, authority, references = the gateway references, late, actor). close writes SEC_INCIDENT_CLOSED only when its update changed the row (REPORTED to CLOSED). NEW SecurityIncidentCatalogueEventsH2Test. Tests NOT_RUN. | all"
Add-Content -Encoding UTF8 -Path "$h\WAVE4-SYNC-BOARD.md" -Value $change
$info = "$ts | W4-A/B61 | INFO | Decision 299, DPDP_BREACH_REPORTED below 97 percent, not coded until answered. Evidence: SANGAM.md OJ-06 step 7 (line 6063) 'within T0+72 h: if personal data, notice to affected data principals and Board report'. The code doing that is BreachIncidentService.submitDetailedReport: the 72 h detailed report to the pack's breach authority (IN pack: DPB, DPDP s.8(6) r.7), whose content carries the notices to data principals (affected and notified counts); it writes CMP_BREACH_DETAILED_REPORT today. BreachIncidentService is jurisdiction-generic: the EU-GDPR and US-HIPAA packs use the same method for their own authority, where a DPDP name would be false. Question: (A) write DPDP_BREACH_REPORTED in submitDetailedReport only when the tenant's pack is the IN pack (breach authority DPB, DPDP s.8(6)), with breach, authority, ref, late, principals affected and notified, contentHash, actor; other packs keep only CMP_BREACH_DETAILED_REPORT. (B) write it for every pack. (C) write it at notifyAuthority (the initial intimation without delay) instead. My proposal is A. Also for the record, not coded (no feature, nothing invented): OJ-06 step 8 says closure requires RCA and lessons; IncidentReportingService.close has no RCA or lessons today, so SEC_INCIDENT_CLOSED records the existing REPORTED to CLOSED change only. | coordinator, owner"
Add-Content -Encoding UTF8 -Path "$h\WAVE4-SYNC-BOARD.md" -Value $info
$req = "$ts | W4-A/B61 | REQUEST | To W4-K (decision 299, files in sangam-packs that W4-A must not edit), and INFO to the coordinator: the three R61 names assigned to W4-A have their work in sangam-packs, not in sangam-compliance (RetentionScheduler is DPDP purpose erasure and HierarchyRetention is engine history purge; neither reviews records nor transfers to NAI). What exists: (1) RECORD_REVIEWED: packs/records/sangam-record-retention.bpmn user task rr_decide 'Record review (Public Records Rules r.9)', decision in reviewDecision (retain, transferNai, destroy) recorded by ActorRecorderListener on complete. (2) RECORD_TRANSFERRED_NAI: the same process, service task rr_nai 'Transfer to National Archives (PDF/A)', ConnectorCallDelegate connector archive.nai operation transfer mode submit, result prefix nai, reached from the review or from the appraisal (appraisalDecision transferNai). (3) RTI_REQUEST_LINKED: the feature exists (W4-M saw no emitter, not no feature): packs/p2-file-movement/sangam-p2-file-movement.bpmn message sangam.rtiLinked starts event subprocess p2_rti 'RTI request linked', whose task p2_rtiHold runs CaseRecordDelegate op LEGAL_HOLD (LEGAL_HOLD_SET); SANGAM.md J-P2-E10 names RTI_REQUEST_LINKED plus LEGAL_HOLD_SET for this step. Proposal for W4-K: CaseRecordDelegate gains ops REVIEW (RECORD_REVIEWED: fileNo, decision, retentionCategory, next review date when retained, actor) and RTI_LINK (RTI_REQUEST_LINKED: fileNo, the RTI reference from the message, actor), written through Vars.audit in the engine transaction like RETENTION_CLASSIFIED; rr_decide is followed by an REVIEW step and p2_rti by an RTI_LINK step before p2_rtiHold; RECORD_TRANSFERRED_NAI is written in the transaction that settles the archive.nai transfer as succeeded (fileNo, nai reference, actor), not when the submit is only requested. W4-K please ACK or take the three names; I write nothing in sangam-packs. | W4-K, coordinator"
